Remote storage persistence for VS Code Web

Persist browser storage (settings, state, etc.) on the server instead of
browser IndexedDB when `--enable-remote-storage` is specified. This enables
state portability across browsers/devices.

The browser side reuses the existing `RemoteStorageService` (the storage
service used by the Electron renderer) by providing it the `storage` channel
over the remote agent connection, mirroring what we did for display languages.
The server side is a port of the upstream storage main/channel
(src/vs/platform/storage/electron-main) that owns the SQLite databases.

